-- title:
--   Integral j-charts of X₁(Mp) reduce into the Igusa function field
-- statement:
--   Fix a prime $p$, a natural number $M$ with $5 \le M$ and $p \nmid M$, and a characteristic-zero field $L$ that is a cyclotomic extension of $\mathbb{Q}$ of order $p$, together with a primitive $p$-th root of unity $\zeta \in L$. Let $K$ be an intermediate field of $L \subseteq \mathrm{LaurentSeries}\ L$ equal to [`ModularCurve.laurentBaseChange L (ModularCurve.x1FunctionField (M * p))`](def/ModularCurve_LaurentCoeff.html#L103), i.e. the subfield generated over $L$ by the image under [`ModularCurve.coeffEmb L`](def/ModularCurve_LaurentCoeff.html#L81) of the function field `x1FunctionFieldC ℚ (M * p)`. Let $A$ be a discrete valuation domain with $L$ as fraction field, with $p$ in its maximal ideal and $\zeta$ in the image of $A$, and let $K$ be an $A$-algebra compatibly with $L$. Let $j \in K$ be nonzero with Laurent expansion [`ModularCurve.coeffEmb L ModularCurve.jq`](def/ModularCurve_LaurentCoeff.html#L81), the image of $q^{-1}$ times the integral $j$-numerator series. Let $k$ be an algebraically closed $A$-algebra field of characteristic $p$, and let $w$ be an `IntegralWeightOneForm k M`, that is, a weight-one modular form on $\Gamma_1(M)$ together with an integral power series realising its $q$-expansion whose reduction `intSeriesC k` is nonzero; write $L_0 =$ [`ModularCurve.igusaFunctionFieldX1C k M w`](def/ModularCurve_IgusaFunctionFieldX1.html#L35) for the associated Igusa function field inside $\mathrm{LaurentSeries}\ k$. Then there exist $t \in L_0$ and $k$-algebra homomorphisms $\theta_{\mathrm{fin}} : k \otimes_A$ `chartAlgFin A ↥K j` $\to$ `chartRing k {t}` and $\theta_{\infty} : k \otimes_A$ `chartAlgInf A ↥K j` $\to$ `chartRing k {t⁻¹}` (targets: the elements of $L_0$ integral over $k[t]$, respectively over $k[t^{-1}]$) such that: the Laurent expansion of $t$ is [`ModularCurve.jqModC k`](def/ModularCurve_JqCoeff.html#L15), namely $q^{-1}$ times the mod-$p$ reduction of the $j$-numerator; $\theta_{\mathrm{fin}}(1 \otimes$ `jChartFin A ↥K j`$) = t$ and $\theta_{\infty}(1 \otimes$ `jInvChartInf A ↥K j`$) = t^{-1}$; for all $b$ in the finite chart algebra, $b'$ in the infinite chart algebra and $n \in \mathbb{N}$ with $b = b' j^{n}$ in $K$, one has $\theta_{\mathrm{fin}}(1 \otimes b) = \theta_{\infty}(1 \otimes b')\, t^{n}$; for either chart algebra and all $x, y \in A[[q]]$ with $y$ nonzero modulo the maximal ideal of $A$ and with $b \cdot y = x$ as Laurent series over $L$, the Laurent expansion of the image of $1 \otimes b$ equals the quotient of the images of $x$ and $y$ in $k[[q]]$; and the kernel of each of $\theta_{\mathrm{fin}}$, $\theta_{\infty}$ is the ideal generated by those pure tensors $1 \otimes b$ that it annihilates.
--
--   This is the comparison, in characteristic $p$, between the two $j$-charts of the integral model of $X(\Gamma_1(M) \cap \Gamma_1(p))$ over the ring of integers of $\mathbb{Q}(\zeta_p)$ localised at $p$ and the affine chart rings of the Igusa curve attached to a weight-one form: the charts map to the Igusa curve by Gauss reduction of $q$-expansions, with $j \mapsto \bar\jmath$, compatibly on the overlap and with kernels generated by pure tensors. It is obtained from the pair of valuation subrings produced by [`ModularCurve.XOneP.exists_valuationSubring_pair_x1_mul`](thm.html#ModularCurve.XOneP.exists_valuationSubring_pair_x1_mul), and is used by the variant adding surjectivity of the two maps and by the construction of the curve-model pair whose special fibre is birational to the two-chart integral model.
